cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Tool-Result Errors in Language-Model Agents: A Fixed-Prefix Measurement Study of Switches, Silent Propagation, and Recovery"
abstract: >-
  Fixed-prefix measurement study of how the content of a real tool
  observation changes a language-model agent's next decision. 800 frozen
  tau-bench prefixes (400 airline, 400 retail), five observation arms,
  three open-weight 8-9B models, 21,611 generations. Confirmatory analysis
  complete: pooled conditional-logit slope 0.877 [0.770, 0.998] with three
  failed gate criteria (parser 1.55% vs 1%, severity s2/s3 88.3% vs 90%,
  crude recovery on the semantic risk set 24.4/32.9/21.3% vs 50%); no causal or content-sensitivity
  claim. Dataset v1.0.1 staged for DOI release (scrubbed, redacted derived data
  only; one scrubber-artifact identity is replaced at build time).
